{# Load-more partial — rendered by GET /feed/more?cursor=<opaque>&shown=<N>.
   htmx target: hx-target="#load-more-trigger" hx-swap="outerHTML"
   Variables: lots (list[LotUserViewModel]), next_cursor (str|None), shown_total (int)

   Behaviour:
   - Emits lot cards via _lot_poster.html.jinja (same template as the initial feed).
   - When next_cursor is present: injects a fresh #load-more-trigger div (inside the
     existing <section class="zone">) so the user can keep paging.  outerHTML on
     #load-more-trigger replaces only the trigger — the new cards become its siblings
     inside the same zone section, matching the initial-page DOM nesting.
   - When absent (last page): emits a hidden sentinel so outerHTML still removes the
     trigger cleanly (empty body would be a no-op swap in HTMX 1.9).

   Lot counter: NOT managed here.  The filter-bar #feed-lot-count element shows the
   true total from DB (set at initial render via build_feed_context / lot_query.count).
   Live lot.new SSE events are handled client-side by incrementLotCounters() in app.js
   which increments all .js-lot-count elements.  load-more must NOT touch the counter
   — overwriting it with a smaller "shown so far" value would corrupt the true total.

   Session context: mirrors SessionStubForFilter from filters.py (expired=False by
   default; the user is actively browsing so the session is considered active).
   Matches the stub used by POST /filters/view so gating logic is consistent.

   SSE coexistence: SSE swaps arrive on section#feed-zone-list with afterbegin
   (lot.new) and on span#lot-status-listener with hx-swap="none" (lot.status);
   load-more fragments are appended here at the bottom via outerHTML on
   #load-more-trigger.  The two operations target disjoint DOM regions and never
   collide.
#}

{# Session stub mirrors SessionStubForFilter in filters.py: expired=False so that
   "Открыть" buttons render the same way on loaded pages as on the initial render. #}
{% set session = namespace(expired=false, expires_soon=false, expires_at_hhmm="") %}

{% for lot in lots %}
  {% include "partials/_lot_poster.html.jinja" %}
{% endfor %}

{% if next_cursor %}
<div id="load-more-trigger"
     hx-get="/feed/more?cursor={{ next_cursor | urlencode }}&amp;shown={{ shown_total }}"
     hx-target="#load-more-trigger"
     hx-swap="outerHTML"
     hx-trigger="click from:#load-more-btn">
  <button id="load-more-btn" class="btn btn--ghost btn--full" type="button"
          style="justify-content: center; padding: 12px 16px;">
    <span style="display:inline-flex; gap:8px; align-items:center;">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
      Показать ещё
    </span>
  </button>
</div>
{% else %}
{# Last page: emit a hidden sentinel so outerHTML swap cleanly removes the trigger
   even when no cards were produced (empty body would be a no-op in HTMX 1.9). #}
<span hidden></span>
{% endif %}

{# OOB counter removed: #feed-lot-count now shows the true total from DB
   (set at initial render via build_feed_context / lot_query.count).
   Live lot.new SSE events increment all .js-lot-count elements client-side.
   load-more must NOT overwrite the counter — it would replace the true total
   with the smaller "shown so far" value (ddpf+hke7). #}
